---
// Epley & Schroeder's reversal, and only the reversal: riders put talking to
// a stranger last and it came first. The release publishes no effect sizes,
// so the figure deliberately plots no magnitudes and ranks no other
// condition --- drawing a full three-way chart would be inventing data the
// source doesn't have.
//
// Captions are HTML under the SVG rather than <text> inside it. A
// role="img" element makes its children presentational, so a provenance
// note written into the SVG would be invisible to a screen reader --- and
// provenance is exactly the thing that shouldn't depend on being able to
// see the picture.
---

<figure class="fig-forecast">
  <svg
    class="fig"
    viewBox="0 0 900 225"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Riders predicted that talking to a stranger would be the worst of the three commutes. It was the best."
  >
    <text class="head" x="180" y="26" text-anchor="middle">what riders predicted</text>
    <text class="head" x="720" y="26" text-anchor="middle">what actually happened</text>

    <line class="axis" x1="180" y1="52" x2="180" y2="212" />
    <line class="axis" x1="720" y1="52" x2="720" y2="212" />

    <text class="rank" x="150" y="66" text-anchor="end">best</text>
    <text class="rank" x="150" y="206" text-anchor="end">worst</text>
    <text class="rank" x="750" y="66">best</text>
    <text class="rank" x="750" y="206">worst</text>

    <line class="flip" x1="180" y1="200" x2="720" y2="60" />
    <circle class="dot" cx="180" cy="200" r="11" />
    <circle class="dot" cx="720" cy="60" r="11" />

    <text class="callout" x="450" y="168" text-anchor="middle">talking to a stranger</text>
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    <span
      >Epley &amp; Schroeder (2014) — nine experiments, commuter trains and
      buses. Three conditions: talk to a stranger, sit in solitude, ride as
      normal. Same answer every time.</span
    >
    <span class="provenance"
      >Diagram made for this lecture, not reproduced from the paper —
      generated with AI.</span
    >
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-forecast {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .fig {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-block: 0.5rem;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .head {
    fill: var(--at-light-grey);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .axis {
    stroke: var(--at-divider);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .rank {
    fill: var(--at-text-secondary);
    font-size: 17px;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .flip {
    stroke: var(--at-primary);
    stroke-width: 5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }

  .dot {
    fill: var(--at-primary);
  }

  .callout {
    fill: var(--at-primary);
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }

  .provenance {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
